@format 1
@id section-creation.common.apply-created-state
@title Apply created section state
@section Section creation
@area Common
@entry apply-plan
@summary Apply an accepted creation plan, synchronously update Split visuals and history, save section records to the sidecar, then perform the caller-specific creation log.
@related section-creation.add-at-cursor, section-creation.set-start-creates-section, section-creation.set-end-creates-section, section-creation.split-selected-section
@tag section
@tag split
@tag creation
@tag persistence
@tag history

@alias segment = Cadroue.Application.LSegment
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias history = Cadroue.Application.LHistory
@alias sidecar = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LSidecarStore

[apply-plan] Accepted section-list plan <input>
~ This starts with accepted section-list plan.
[Technical explanation]
= LSegmentAdd, LSegmentStartSet, LSegmentEndSet, or LSegmentDivide has obtained a replacement list and active index from LPiece planning.
> replace-state

[replace-state] Replace segment state <process>
~ This step handles replace segment state.
[Technical explanation]
- Clear the current internal pieces, copy the accepted list, set the active index, and synchronously invoke LSegmentChange with a snapshot @ segment.LSegmentApply(...)
> flow-change

[flow-change] Update Flow section presentation <process>
~ This step handles update Flow section presentation.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSegmentHandle marks pFlowSegmentFired, updates the Viewfinder and Map section geometry, and invokes PFlowSectionChange @ flow.PFlowSegmentHandle(...)
> section-panel

[section-panel] Rebuild the Sections panel <process>
~ This step handles rebuild the Sections panel.
[Technical explanation]
- The Split PSection subscriber receives the changed list; because creation changes the list it rebuilds the count and rows with the new active selection @ panel.PSectionUpdateHandle(...)
> workspace-history

[workspace-history] Record undo history <process>
~ This step handles record undo history.
[Technical explanation]
- The PWorkspace subscriber snapshots sections, selection, and export state; LHistoryAdd stores the changed state unless history is currently being applied or the state matches the present entry @ workspace.PWorkspaceSectionHandle(...)
@ workspace.PWorkspaceHistoryAdd(...)
@ history.LHistoryAdd(...)
> sidecar-save

[sidecar-save] Persist section records <process>
~ This step handles persist section records.
[Technical explanation]
- After LSegmentChange returns, LSegmentApply calls LSegmentSave; with a source path and outside restore mode, the configured save seam attempts to write the current section records into the media sidecar; the bool returned by LSidecarSectionsSave is not consumed by the Action seam @ segment.LSegmentApply(...) / LSegmentSave after LSegmentChange
@ segment.LSegmentSave(...)
@ sidecar.LSidecarSectionsSave(...)
> caller-log

[caller-log] Resume the creation caller <decision>
~ The program checks resume the creation caller.
[Technical explanation]
= The synchronous LSegmentApply call has completed its UI/history/persistence consequences before control returns to the originating PFlow method.
? "Add at cursor" > add-log
? "Set Start created" > start-log
? "Set End created" > end-log
? "Split selected section" > split-log

[add-log] Log Add creation <output>
~ This path ends with log Add creation.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSectionAdd records added only when the synchronous change set pFlowSegmentFired @ flow.PFlowSectionAdd(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)

[start-log] Log Set Start creation <output>
~ This path ends with log Set Start creation.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowStartSet receives Added=true and records the selected section as added @ flow.PFlowStartSet(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)

[end-log] Log Set End creation <output>
~ This path ends with log Set End creation.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowEndSet receives Added=true and records the selected section as added @ flow.PFlowEndSet(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)

[split-log] Log both split halves <output>
~ This path ends with log both split halves.
[Technical explanation]
- PFlowSectionDivide reads the selected left-half index and records the left half followed by the new right half @ flow.PFlowSectionDivide(...)
@ flow.PFlowSectionRecord(...)
